Vendored Solidity sources (contracts/vendor/, see contracts/vendor/README.md)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
* OpenZeppelin Contracts 5.6.1. Licence: MIT
  (contracts/vendor/@openzeppelin/contracts/LICENSE).
* Ethereum Attestation Service contracts 1.9.0. Licence: MIT
  (contracts/vendor/@ethereum-attestation-service/eas-contracts/LICENSE).
* ERC-4337 EntryPoint v0.8 (eth-infinitism account-abstraction), core/*.sol.
  Licence: GPL-3.0 (contracts/vendor/@account-abstraction/contracts/LICENSE).
  contracts/build.js compiles EntryPoint.sol; its bytecode is written to
  build/EntryPoint_sol_EntryPoint.bin and embedded in the ternchain binary,
  which deploys it as a separate contract on a devnet. We treat the embedded
  EntryPoint bytecode as a separate work aggregated with ternchain ("mere
  aggregation"): its complete source is in contracts/vendor/ under GPL-3.0.
  Before a mainnet we may switch to the canonical deployed EntryPoint or
  predeploy it in genesis instead of embedding it.

Cryptographic schemes
---------------------
* The secret-vote circuit follows the Semaphore v4 scheme (Semaphore is MIT
  licensed). No Semaphore source code is copied into this repository; the
  circuits are written with gnark.

Own Solidity
------------
* contracts/*.sol: Apache-2.0, except the gnark-exported verifiers
  (PoolVerifier.sol, VoteVerifier.sol: MIT, as generated).
* examples/*.sol: MIT.

The zk proving and verifying keys in internal/zk/keys/ come from a
single-party development setup. They are not secure for anything of value:
whoever ran the setup can forge proofs (see PRIVACY.md and SECURITY.md).
